{"model": "mtp_like", "subset": "icc_backchannel", "task": "backchannel", "sid": "51", "mode": "decision", "duration_s": 71.202, "end_time": 76.834, "gt_user_speech_s": 71.18, "spoke": true, "formal_turn_by_audio": true, "first_speech_start": 11.592, "audible_within_input": true, "speech_beyond_input_s": 0, "speech_intervals": [[11.592, 59.816], [64.108, 66.43], [70.914, 76.834]], "n_turns": 14, "n_decisions": 82, "compute_s": 26.1, "max_decision_s": 1.714, "tts_compute_s": 63.754, "stt_s": 0.803, "stt_partial_s": 0.612, "stt_final_s": 0.191, "stt_calls": 115, "floor_compute_s": 1.1922, "yield_compute_s": 0.3155, "asr_settle_latency_s": 0.6000000000000085, "barge_ins": [{"speech_onset": 16.7, "stop_at": 25.352, "reaction_s": 0.913, "flush_before_playback": true}, {"speech_onset": 24.3, "stop_at": 49.153, "reaction_s": 0.062, "flush_before_playback": true}, {"speech_onset": 36.5, "stop_at": 48.403, "reaction_s": 0.067, "flush_before_playback": true}, {"speech_onset": 56.7, "stop_at": 62.632, "reaction_s": 0.945, "flush_before_playback": true}, {"speech_onset": 59.5, "stop_at": 59.816, "reaction_s": 0.316, "played_before_stop_s": 1.755, "would_have_played_s": 3.44, "asr_settle_s": 0.5}, {"speech_onset": 65.0, "stop_at": 66.43, "reaction_s": 1.43, "played_before_stop_s": 0.892, "would_have_played_s": 13.44, "asr_settle_s": 0.6}, {"speech_onset": 66.5, "stop_at": 67.03, "reaction_s": 0.421, "flush_before_playback": true}], "utt_finalized": 22, "utt_skipped": {"too_short": 1}, "audio_beyond_input_s": 5.632, "tts_capped": 3, "tts_capped_words": 75, "paused_floor_take": null, "interrupt_span": null, "post_interrupt_text": "", "took_floor_after_interrupt": false, "tags": ["user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_finish_speaking:inaudible", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_finish_speaking", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty", "user_is_speaking:empty"], "turns": [{"start": 11.592, "end": 25.352, "natural_end": 25.352, "dur": 13.76, "text": "That's a deep question. If laws or moral decisions were based solely on what people feel, we'd end up with chaos—because feelings vary so widely. True justice and morality need consistency, fairness, and reasoning, not just popularity or", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 38, "stopped": false}, {"start": 25.352, "end": 25.352, "natural_end": 38.552, "dur": 0.0, "text": "Exactly. Morals and laws should be grounded in reason, fairness, and universal principles—not just what people feel. Feelings are valid, but they can be subjective. A just system needs to balance empathy with consistency.<|im_end|>", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 34, "stopped": true}, {"start": 17.713, "end": 33.473, "natural_end": 33.473, "dur": 15.76, "text": "True. Revenge is personal and destructive—it fuels anger, not healing. A just system must aim for fairness, accountability, and restoration, not retribution. That’s why justice should serve peace, not satisfy anger.<|im_end|>", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 31, "stopped": false}, {"start": 33.473, "end": 35.393, "natural_end": 35.393, "dur": 1.92, "text": "Sure, go on! I'm listening. 😊<|im_end|>", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 6, "stopped": false}, {"start": 35.393, "end": 49.153, "natural_end": 49.153, "dur": 13.76, "text": "That's a powerful point. If justice isn't equally distributed, then it's not truly just—no matter how well-intentioned the system may seem. True justice requires fairness, consistency, and equal treatment under the law. When people", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 34, "stopped": false}, {"start": 49.153, "end": 49.153, "natural_end": 63.953, "dur": 0.0, "text": "You're absolutely right—disparities in justice systems, especially regarding racial groups, are real and deeply concerning. Studies show that Black individuals are often disproportionately affected by policing, sentencing, and incarceration. This isn't just a statistical issue—it", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 35, "stopped": true}, {"start": 32.563, "end": 48.403, "natural_end": 48.403, "dur": 15.84, "text": "Yes, that's well documented. Across multiple states, Black people are more likely than white people to receive harsher sentences for the same crimes—despite similar levels of criminal behavior. This disparity reflects systemic biases, unequal treatment, and historical", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 37, "stopped": false}, {"start": 48.403, "end": 48.403, "natural_end": 62.243, "dur": 0.0, "text": "Good point—disparities don’t automatically justify or eliminate the death penalty. But they do raise serious ethical and moral questions: if the system is flawed, who is it serving? And can a punishment that’s applied unequally still", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 36, "stopped": true}, {"start": 47.752, "end": 62.632, "natural_end": 62.632, "dur": 14.88, "text": "Exactly. The moral question isn’t just about fairness in application—it’s about whether the death penalty itself aligns with justice, dignity, and human rights. If it risks dehumanizing, or if it’s applied unfairly, then it challenges", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 35, "stopped": false}, {"start": 62.632, "end": 62.632, "natural_end": 78.392, "dur": 0.0, "text": "That’s a powerful and fundamental point. The idea of \"killing someone\" as a form of justice is deeply moral and controversial. Most ethical frameworks—whether utilitarian, deontological, or humanistic—question whether taking a life", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 32, "stopped": true}, {"start": 57.745, "end": 59.816, "natural_end": 61.185, "dur": 2.07, "text": "Bye! Thanks for the thoughtful conversation. 🙌<|im_end|>", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 7, "stopped": true}, {"start": 64.108, "end": 66.43, "natural_end": 77.548, "dur": 2.321, "text": "I get you—what you're saying is that when the death penalty is applied disproportionately, especially based on race, it’s not just unfair, it’s a moral failure. And that’s a powerful argument against it. Thanks for sharing.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 36, "stopped": true}, {"start": 67.03, "end": 67.03, "natural_end": 76.63, "dur": 0.0, "text": "Exactly. When justice is driven by revenge instead of reason, it loses its moral foundation. The death penalty, in that light, becomes a tool of anger—not", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 26, "stopped": true}, {"start": 70.914, "end": 76.834, "natural_end": 76.834, "dur": 5.92, "text": "Great point. Feelings of revenge and racial bias don’t just influence decisions—they distort them.", "tag": "user_finish_speaking", "kind": "speech", "n_words": 14, "stopped": false}], "user_pieces": [{"kind": "partial", "text": "Clearly", "t_start": 1.84, "t_end": 2.6, "t_avail": 3.2, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "received the", "t_start": 2.6, "t_end": 3.16, "t_avail": 3.8000000000000003, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "death penalty, but", "t_start": 3.16, "t_end": 3.86, "t_avail": 4.4, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "if you think about it, if you", "t_start": 3.88, "t_end": 5.3, "t_avail": 5.800000000000001, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "base", "t_start": 5.28, "t_end": 5.6, "t_avail": 6.6000000000000005, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "final", "text": "any law...", "t_start": 5.62, "t_end": 6.98, "t_avail": 7.0, "ends_turn": true, "utt": 0}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "or moral", "t_start": 7.0, "t_end": 7.4, "t_avail": 8.200000000000001, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 1}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "decision based on what", "t_start": 7.4, "t_end": 8.2, "t_avail": 9.0, "ends_turn": false, "utt": 1}, {"kind": "partial", "text": "other people", "t_start": 8.22, "t_end": 8.